IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uro-nouns`

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): PART 7, ARTICLES 32 AND 33, WITH SCHEDULE 13 (UNIVERSAL CREDIT).
-- Layer 1. Article 32 amends the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 and article 33 the Universal Credit (Transitional
-- Provisions) Regulations 2014; neither is among the inputs. Every figure the Order states is a value.
-- Dates: arts 32 and 33 come into force on the first day of the beneficiary's first assessment period to commence on or
-- after 6th April 2026 (art 1(3)(n)): uro-part1-intro.

§ `Article 32 -- Universal Credit`

§§ `Article 32(1) -- regulation 22: deduction of income and work allowance`

-- "for 684.00, in each place where it occurs, substitute 710.00": one pair, however many places
-- src:438 | (1) In the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations (deduction of income and work allowance)—
-- src:439 | (a) for “£684.00”, in each place where it occurs, substitute “£710.00”; and
@ref art 32(1)(a) (src:438-439)
`art 32(1)(a): the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations, the sum of 684.00 in each place where it occurs` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 684.00, 710.00

-- src:440 | (b) for “£411.00”, in each place where it occurs, substitute “£427.00”.
@ref art 32(1)(b) (src:440)
`art 32(1)(b): the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations, the sum of 411.00 in each place where it occurs` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 411.00, 427.00

@ref art 32(1) (src:438-440)
DECLARE `a sum in the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `Universal Credit regulation 22 table sum of 684.00`
    `Universal Credit regulation 22 table sum of 411.00`

@ref art 32(1) (src:438-440)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sum in the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations`
GIVETH A `a sum and its replacement`
`art 32(1): the replaced and the replacing sum` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `Universal Credit regulation 22 table sum of 684.00` THEN `art 32(1)(a): the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations, the sum of 684.00 in each place where it occurs`
    WHEN `Universal Credit regulation 22 table sum of 411.00` THEN `art 32(1)(b): the table in regulation 22 of the Universal Credit Regulations, the sum of 411.00 in each place where it occurs`


§§ `Article 32(2) -- regulation 36: the amounts of the elements in Schedule 13`

-- (2): the amounts in the regulation 36 table for the elements set out in Schedule 13 are those of Schedule 13 to this
-- Order, encoded below.

§§ `Article 32(3) -- paragraph 14(1) of Schedule 4: housing cost contributions`

-- src:442 | (3) In paragraph 14(1) of Schedule 4 to the Universal Credit Regulations (amount of housing cost contributions) for “£93.02” substitute “£96.55”.
@ref art 32(3) (src:442)
`art 32(3): paragraph 14(1) of Schedule 4 to the Universal Credit Regulations, the amount of housing cost contributions` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 93.02, 96.55


§ `Article 33 -- Amendment of the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014`

§§ `Article 33(a) -- paragraph 5 of Schedule 2: claimants previously entitled to a severe disability premium`

-- src:444 | In the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014—
-- src:445 | (a) in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 (claimants previously entitled to a severe disability premium)—
-- src:446 | (i) for “£143.37”, in both places where it occurs, substitute “£148.82”;
@ref art 33(a)(i) (src:444-446)
`art 33(a)(i): paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 143.37 in both places where it occurs` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 143.37, 148.82

-- src:447 | (ii) for “£340.50”, in both places where it occurs, substitute “£353.44”; and
@ref art 33(a)(ii) (src:447)
`art 33(a)(ii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 340.50 in both places where it occurs` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 340.50, 353.44

-- src:448 | (iii) for “£483.88” substitute “£502.27”; and
@ref art 33(a)(iii) (src:448)
`art 33(a)(iii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 483.88` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 483.88, 502.27

@ref art 33(a) (src:444-448)
DECLARE `a sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014` IS ONE OF
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 2 paragraph 5 sum of 143.37`
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 2 paragraph 5 sum of 340.50`
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 2 paragraph 5 sum of 483.88`

@ref art 33(a) (src:444-448)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014`
GIVETH A `a sum and its replacement`
`art 33(a): the replaced and the replacing sum` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 2 paragraph 5 sum of 143.37` THEN `art 33(a)(i): paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 143.37 in both places where it occurs`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 2 paragraph 5 sum of 340.50` THEN `art 33(a)(ii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 340.50 in both places where it occurs`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 2 paragraph 5 sum of 483.88` THEN `art 33(a)(iii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 2 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 483.88`


§§ `Article 33(b) -- paragraph 5 of Schedule 3: additional amounts for claimants previously entitled to an enhanced disability premium, a disability premium, a disabled child premium or a disabled child element in addition to a severe disability premium`

-- src:449 | (b) in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 (additional amounts for claimants previously entitled to an enhanced disability premium, a disability premium, a disabled child premium or a disabled child element in addition to a severe disability premium)—
