-- src:451 | (ii) for “£186.64” substitute “£193.73”;
@ref art 33(b)(ii) (src:451)
`art 33(b)(ii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 186.64` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 186.64, 193.73

-- src:452 | (iii) for “£192.07”, in both places where it occurs, substitute “£199.37”;
@ref art 33(b)(iii) (src:452)
`art 33(b)(iii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 192.07 in both places where it occurs` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 192.07, 199.37

-- src:453 | (iv) for “£130.22” substitute “£135.17”; and
@ref art 33(b)(iv) (src:453)
`art 33(b)(iv): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 130.22` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 130.22, 135.17

-- src:454 | (v) for “£266.94” substitute “£277.08”.
@ref art 33(b)(v) (src:454)
`art 33(b)(v): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 266.94` MEANS `a sum and its replacement` OF 266.94, 277.08

@ref art 33(b) (src:449-454)
DECLARE `a sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014` IS ONE OF
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 91.15`
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 186.64`
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 192.07`
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 130.22`
    `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 266.94`

@ref art 33(b) (src:449-454)
GIVEN `which one` IS A `a sum in paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014`
GIVETH A `a sum and its replacement`
`art 33(b): the replaced and the replacing sum` `which one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which one`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 91.15` THEN `art 33(b)(i): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 91.15`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 186.64` THEN `art 33(b)(ii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 186.64`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 192.07` THEN `art 33(b)(iii): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 192.07 in both places where it occurs`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 130.22` THEN `art 33(b)(iv): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 130.22`
    WHEN `Universal Credit (Transitional) Schedule 3 paragraph 5 sum of 266.94` THEN `art 33(b)(v): paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 to the Universal Credit (Transitional Provisions) Regulations 2014, the sum of 266.94`


§ `Schedule 13 to the Order -- amounts of certain elements specified in the table in regulation 36 of the Universal Credit Regulations`

-- The amounts are for each assessment period. Which child is the first, and whether a child is "qualifying", is for the
-- Universal Credit Regulations; the encoding takes the child's place in the order as a number.

-- out of text: Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (which child is first; 'qualifying young person'): the child's place in the order is an input.
-- src:441 | (2) The amounts specified in the table in regulation 36 of the Universal Credit Regulations (table showing amounts of elements) in relation to the elements set out in Schedule 13 to this Order are as set out in that Schedule.
@ref art 32(2) (src:441)
-- src:768 | | Child element— |
-- src:769 | | | first child or qualifying young person | £351.88 |
-- src:770 | | | second and each subsequent child or qualifying young person | £303.94 |
@ref Sch 13 (src:768-770)
GIVEN `the place of the child or qualifying young person in the order of the children` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 13: the child element for the child or qualifying young person` `the place of the child or qualifying young person in the order of the children` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place of the child or qualifying young person in the order of the children` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 351.88   -- first child or qualifying young person
        IF `the place of the child or qualifying young person in the order of the children` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST 303.94   -- second and each subsequent
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:771 | | Additional amount for disabled child or qualifying young person— |
-- src:772 | | | lower rate | £164.79 |
-- src:773 | | | higher rate | £514.71 |
@ref Sch 13 (src:771-773)
DECLARE `a rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` IS ONE OF
    `the lower rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person`
    `the higher rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person`

-- out of text: Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (disabled child additional amount): which rate applies is an input.
@ref Sch 13 (src:771-773)
GIVEN `which rate` IS A `a rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 13: the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` `which rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which rate`
    WHEN `the lower rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` THEN 164.79   -- lower rate
    WHEN `the higher rate of the additional amount for a disabled child or qualifying young person` THEN 514.71   -- higher rate

-- src:774 | | Carer element | £209.34 |
@ref Sch 13 (src:774)
`Sch 13: the carer element` MEANS 209.34

-- out of text: Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (childcare costs element): the number of children is an input.
-- src:775 | | Childcare costs element— | |
-- src:776 | | | maximum amount for one child | £1,071.09 |
-- src:777 | | | maximum amount for two or more children | £1,836.16 |
@ref Sch 13 (src:775-777)
GIVEN `the number of children` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 13: the maximum amount of the childcare costs element` `the number of children` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of children` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 1071.09   -- maximum amount for one child
        IF `the number of children` AT LEAST 2 THEN JUST 1836.16   -- maximum amount for two or more children
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
